# Descriptor for this agent. agent-mgr supplies everything else.
#
# Every key here is optional -- agent-mgr derives all of them from the agent's
# name. Set one only to override the convention, and say why.
#
#   AGENT_HOME       default ~/.hermes-<name>
#   AGENT_CONTAINER  default hermes-<name>
#   AGENT_PROJECT    default hermes-<name>
#   AGENT_TZ         default America/Los_Angeles
#   AGENT_IMAGE      default the digest in agent-mgr's runtime/image.ref
#   AGENT_CONFIG     default config.yaml, resolved against this directory
#
# Two more, both optional and unset by default. Each names a script in this
# repo, resolved against this directory:
#
#   AGENT_RESTORE_HOOK   `agent-mgr restore` runs it after its own installs --
#                        an agent's own restore step, such as seeding a corpus.
#                        agent-mgr sequences it so that one command is the whole
#                        deploy.
#
#   AGENT_PRE_TRANSITION this agent's veto on being stopped or replaced, for an
#                        agent that must not be bounced mid-run. A non-zero exit
#                        refuses, and what that costs depends on who asked:
#                        `up`, `down`, `restart`, `restore` and a transitioning
#                        `compose` passthrough ABORT RED; the reload after a
#                        write -- `install-plugin`, `activate`, `sign-in`,
#                        `add-skill` -- skips the restart and still EXITS GREEN,
#                        since the write itself has already landed.
#
# An instance that needs a derived image or extra mounts adds a
# compose.override.yml beside this file and sets the variables it names here.
